                <pb facs="0408" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3231/997: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-27T23:00:00-03:00">August 27, 1935—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 28—6:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>202. My 200, August 27, 6 p.m. Foreign Minister tells me he had a long discussion
                    with the President and gave him our ideas in full. The President was much
                    impressed and promised to take all possible measures to ensure early
                    ratification.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
